  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "I just installed 2.2 and am trying to do something simple but without success. I wonder if anyone might recognize what I'm doing wrong.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "I'm trying to run the client find utility to get a list of pids: ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "$FEDORA_HOME/client/bin/fedora-find.sh localhost 9080 pid demo http",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "I get the following error:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Starting Fedora Lister...",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "ERROR: java.lang.IllegalArgumentException: Username may not be null",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "It's not clear to me from the documentation how to indicate the username or why it would be necessary. The ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://hostname/fedora/search"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://hostname/fedora/search",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " url works fine.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
