       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/8285187b23d5d8ea87a1ecc2e6d456d6?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBB-1.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Bill Branan",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5d83b5f927bbf40c2c32ceeb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Updated the fedora-find utility to require a username and password, which is passed to FedoraClient, enabling it to work correctly. Requiring credentials for use of the fedora-find utility is expected when API-A authentication is turned on, but these changes require credentials in all cases in order to get around needing to perform a check of the server configuration before operating.</p>",
     "created": "12/Feb/09 6:40 PM",
